  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">
      <i>Ridëtque Saturni Volucris</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2">
      <i>Inuidiam,rabidósque dentes.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3" para="true">
      <i>Hoc, Zastrifelli,tramite prouidus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4">
      <i>Mansura poscis pramia gloria,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5">
      <i>Quum bella te dulci gerentem</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>Propatria laribúsque charis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7" para="true">
      <i>Idem Thalia pellit amor bonos</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>Probare semper Phœbigenum choros:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>Et,Beza quos olim sonauit</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>Doctiloquus graviore pleCtro</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11" para="true">
      <i>Vulgare Versus,&amp; Morauum Orbibus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>Monstrare alumnum Calliopes,sacra</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>Cui Delius lucens Venustat</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>Fronde caput,facilesque Musa,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15" para="true">
      <i>Quem Voce Gallus Neclarea modos</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>Fundentem amanos suspicit,&amp; potens</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17">
      <i>Anglus duellis,accolaque</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>Eridani, rigidúsque Teuto,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19" para="true">
      <i>Et Belga fortis quem Polyhymnia</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>Miti renidens lumine conspicit.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21">
      <i>Et longa cui per bella crescit</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22">
      <i>Dulcisona studium Camane,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23" para="true">
      <i>At,Beza quanuis ludicra nunc Vocet,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24">
      <i>Leuésque gerrascarmina,arundine</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25">
      <i>Qua puriori lusit olim,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="26">
      <i>Et rapidis,nimium seuerus,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="27" para="true">
      <i>Flammis cremari mandet( ad igneas</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Line-end marks: "**" star mark and small "2" are printed at lower right; the star ornament is not text. Some words uncertain in the blackletter-like long-s forms; "Orbibus" reads "Orbibus" in print (possibly "Vrbibus"); "Morauum" as printed. Passage is Latin verse by Beza-era poet; copied from scan, not from memory.</notes>
</page>
